WEBVTT

00:01.501 --> 00:02.877
Me, me! Pick me!

00:02.961 --> 00:04.546
Me, me! I know it!

00:04.629 --> 00:06.256
Let's ask… Hana!

00:06.756 --> 00:07.674
Yes, ma'am!

00:09.384 --> 00:12.429
I'm so glad we asked Shin and Lu
to mind the store today.

00:12.929 --> 00:15.098
I wonder how they're doing.

00:15.181 --> 00:17.308
They're fine… Probably.

00:17.392 --> 00:18.226
SAKAMOTO'S

00:18.309 --> 00:19.310
Hey, Lu!

00:19.394 --> 00:22.605
Stop wearing my apron for dirty tasks!

00:22.689 --> 00:27.193
You make a fuss over everything!
You wash the windows, then!

00:27.277 --> 00:28.319
No way!

00:28.903 --> 00:30.280
Let me be clear.

00:30.780 --> 00:35.326
While Mr. Sakamoto and Ms. Aoi are out,
I'm the one in charge of this place.

00:35.410 --> 00:37.537
Yeah, yeah, whatever.

00:37.620 --> 00:40.331
<i>Shin is like a little kid sometimes…</i>

00:40.832 --> 00:44.252
Anything you want to say to me,
say it to my face, Lu.

00:44.335 --> 00:46.254
You know I can hear it anyway.

00:46.337 --> 00:48.798
I still have freedom of thought.

00:48.882 --> 00:52.343
You're the one
reading my mind without permission.

00:52.427 --> 00:55.764
Yo, got any pork buns you're throwing out?
I'd be happy to help.

00:55.847 --> 00:59.142
Who reads people's minds anyway?
That's totally perverted!

00:59.225 --> 01:01.811
You dumb blond, mind-stalking creep!

01:01.895 --> 01:04.731
Shut up, you apron-stealing drunk!

01:06.483 --> 01:09.736
How could I ever be comfortable around you
knowing you're reading my mind?!

01:13.656 --> 01:15.075
Is that how it is?

01:15.158 --> 01:16.367
Sorry about that.

01:18.453 --> 01:20.914
Hey, shouldn't you stop him?

01:21.414 --> 01:22.373
Who cares?

01:26.419 --> 01:27.629
Mind if I eat these?

01:28.129 --> 01:29.506
You get out of here too.

01:34.886 --> 01:36.262
So annoying.

01:38.306 --> 01:40.767
<i>I've never seen Shin like that…</i>

01:42.185 --> 01:45.855
Back already, huh?
Fine, I'll let you apologize…

01:49.234 --> 01:50.944
SHIN

01:51.027 --> 01:51.861
It's him.

01:52.570 --> 01:53.947
You're coming with us.

03:27.498 --> 03:30.376
JURASSIC BASTARD

03:30.960 --> 03:32.170
Man, what a surprise!

03:32.253 --> 03:35.924
A subject that disappeared from the Lab
11 years ago,

03:36.007 --> 03:38.885
living carefree, in a town like this?

03:38.968 --> 03:41.471
Dyed his hair and everything too.

03:42.472 --> 03:45.725
Hey, Mr. Tanaka,
I don't know how to tell you this, but…

03:45.808 --> 03:47.143
What is it, Seba?

03:47.810 --> 03:49.812
I think we have the wrong person.

03:52.857 --> 03:54.901
Of course it's him!

03:54.984 --> 03:57.153
The nametag says "Shin," plain and simple!

03:57.237 --> 03:59.155
I'll kill you, you little shit!

03:59.239 --> 04:00.240
M'kay, sorry.

04:00.323 --> 04:03.243
Why are we kidnapping the brat anyway?

04:03.826 --> 04:06.204
I don't know the whole story,

04:06.287 --> 04:09.499
but remember how the Lab
used to do experiments to create psychics?

04:10.291 --> 04:12.877
<i>He's the only subject it worked on.</i>

04:12.961 --> 04:15.463
<i>Apparently, he can really read minds.</i>

04:16.631 --> 04:18.675
Talk about creepy, huh?

04:18.758 --> 04:21.678
Your every thought being read at any time?

04:21.761 --> 04:24.472
Who would want to be near someone
that could do that?

04:25.056 --> 04:28.726
I bet no one likes him,
and no one ever will.

04:28.810 --> 04:31.479
What a miserable loser. Ha ha ha!

04:34.691 --> 04:35.858
Mr. Tanaka!

04:35.942 --> 04:37.610
How dare you.

04:38.152 --> 04:40.655
Shin might be dumb and picky and immature,

04:40.738 --> 04:43.199
but he's a much better person than you!

04:43.992 --> 04:47.829
What's wrong with being different
in the first place?

04:47.912 --> 04:49.706
There's nothing miserable about that!

04:49.789 --> 04:51.708
Wait a minute.

04:51.791 --> 04:53.334
What's your name?

04:53.418 --> 04:55.545
Me? I'm Lu Shaotang.

04:55.628 --> 04:56.462
What?

04:56.546 --> 04:58.423
See? I told you so.

04:58.506 --> 05:01.509
You seriously need to listen to people,
Mr. Tanaka.

05:03.636 --> 05:07.682
Oh, well.
I guess I gotta be the bigger man here.

05:08.808 --> 05:11.686
All right, Lu. I'll let you apologize…

05:12.645 --> 05:14.939
Huh? Is she slacking off again?

05:22.947 --> 05:24.198
We're back!

05:24.949 --> 05:26.242
Mr. Sakamoto…

05:28.036 --> 05:29.120
<i>What's going on?</i>

05:30.955 --> 05:33.958
Then, when I got back, Lu was gone.

05:34.542 --> 05:37.670
I'm sorry, sir. This is all my fault!

05:37.754 --> 05:40.256
She's on the highway, heading southwest.

05:40.339 --> 05:42.633
What? Mr. Sakamoto, how do you--

05:42.717 --> 05:43.551
SHIN

05:43.634 --> 05:47.221
<i>The name tag has a GPS in it.</i>

05:47.847 --> 05:49.724
You morons!

05:49.807 --> 05:52.226
They're definitely gonna kill us for this!

05:52.310 --> 05:53.144
Bet.

05:53.227 --> 05:55.521
Get us off this highway now, you slowpoke!

05:55.605 --> 05:57.523
The next exit isn't for 15 kilometers.

05:57.607 --> 06:01.110
Damn it! This is why I hate fieldwork.

06:01.194 --> 06:04.155
I know. Maybe we can pretend
that that's Shin.

06:04.238 --> 06:06.824
We tell them he lost his psychic ability.

06:06.908 --> 06:09.035
They'll notice she's a girl, though.

06:09.118 --> 06:09.952
Crap!

06:10.036 --> 06:11.996
<i>Stupid me.</i>

06:12.080 --> 06:14.957
<i>This is karma</i>
<i>for saying something so mean to Shin.</i>

06:15.625 --> 06:17.668
How could I ever
be comfortable around you?!

06:18.544 --> 06:21.380
<i>I didn't mean that at all.</i>

06:21.464 --> 06:23.216
<i>I wish I could've said sorry…</i>

06:33.893 --> 06:36.437
We'd like our pork bun chef back now.

06:36.521 --> 06:39.690
Shin! Mr. Manager!

06:40.191 --> 06:42.068
What? Is that the real Shin?

06:42.151 --> 06:44.487
It is! It's the kid from the photo, Seba!

06:44.570 --> 06:45.488
Congrats.

06:45.571 --> 06:48.449
We can go back to the Lab
without fearing for our lives!

06:49.784 --> 06:52.203
<i>They're with the Lab?</i>

06:52.286 --> 06:54.122
Get 'em, guys!

06:59.210 --> 07:02.130
Hey there, fatty. Time for a nap!

07:09.220 --> 07:10.388
What?!

07:10.471 --> 07:12.723
Hey, mind if I use some of these?

07:12.807 --> 07:14.809
Sure! As many as you like!

07:20.648 --> 07:22.191
Damn it! You little…

07:22.275 --> 07:24.694
Wow! You guys shooting a movie?

07:24.777 --> 07:25.611
Sure.

07:31.617 --> 07:34.829
Who are those guys? They're insane!

07:34.912 --> 07:36.539
Wait, we lost all of them?

07:36.622 --> 07:37.874
It seems like it.

07:37.957 --> 07:39.876
You'd better stop this!

07:39.959 --> 07:42.962
Apologize before things get worse.

07:43.796 --> 07:45.465
Shut it back there!

07:46.007 --> 07:48.134
If we go back empty-handed,

07:48.217 --> 07:50.344
what'll happen then is so much worse…

07:50.428 --> 07:52.680
You're no exception.
If they don't need you…

07:53.848 --> 07:55.641
Lu, are you all right? Lu!

07:55.725 --> 07:57.810
Seba! Help, Seba!

07:57.894 --> 08:01.606
Fine, I'll do it. Take the wheel for me.

08:08.571 --> 08:11.240
I'd better get paid extra for this.

08:12.533 --> 08:14.160
You want a fight? Okay.

08:14.243 --> 08:16.871
I'm counting on you, Seba!

08:16.954 --> 08:18.289
Yeah, yeah.

08:18.372 --> 08:22.126
Having an incompetent boss
is a lot of work.

08:33.930 --> 08:36.307
Careful, Mr. Sakamoto!

08:38.893 --> 08:42.313
Impressive. You're pretty sharp, huh?

08:44.315 --> 08:45.525
Whoa, scary dude.

08:45.608 --> 08:47.443
Please let me go.

08:54.700 --> 08:55.618
Mr. Sakamoto!

08:58.454 --> 09:02.792
I get why he's "the legendary hit man."
I thought I'd die out there.

09:02.875 --> 09:04.544
Hey, did you get Shin?

09:05.628 --> 09:08.089
Oh yeah, I forgot about that.

09:08.172 --> 09:10.007
Come on, Seba!

09:11.759 --> 09:15.096
Damn it.
Losing the motorbike is a tough blow.

09:15.680 --> 09:18.641
<i>The GPS has stopped at Okutabi.</i>

09:18.724 --> 09:20.309
<i>Who are those men?</i>

09:21.018 --> 09:22.687
I believe they're with the Lab.

09:23.187 --> 09:24.313
<i>The Lab?</i>

09:24.397 --> 09:25.523
Yes.

09:25.606 --> 09:29.110
It's an unauthorized research facility,
and it's where I grew up.

09:30.319 --> 09:31.153
The thing is,

09:33.072 --> 09:35.533
<i>they were a group of weirdos,</i>

09:35.616 --> 09:38.661
<i>but they weren't dangerous like that.</i>

09:39.245 --> 09:40.413
I wonder what happened…

09:41.247 --> 09:42.665
In any case,

09:43.541 --> 09:45.459
we're going to go get Lu back.

09:52.133 --> 09:53.634
So this is the Lab.

09:53.718 --> 09:56.637
Yes. This is a facade they use to hide it.

09:57.305 --> 09:59.515
The Lab is in the basement.

10:00.641 --> 10:03.144
How about we pay a visit
to your childhood home?

10:03.728 --> 10:04.645
Let's do it.

10:16.824 --> 10:18.492
<i>It's pretty crowded.</i>

10:18.576 --> 10:21.579
They operate a normal museum
as their business front.

10:21.662 --> 10:22.496
Hello there!

10:22.580 --> 10:26.167
Welcome to Okutabi Science Museum,
a learning hub for nature and science!

10:26.250 --> 10:28.169
Would you like a souvenir photo?

10:28.252 --> 10:29.754
No, we're in a bit of a hurry.

10:29.837 --> 10:31.547
Come on, what's the harm?

10:31.631 --> 10:33.007
We don't care for photos.

10:33.591 --> 10:35.092
It'll only take a second!

10:35.176 --> 10:36.510
No thank you!

10:36.594 --> 10:38.679
All right, dinosaur poses, please!

10:38.763 --> 10:39.597
Say "roar"!

10:41.932 --> 10:45.394
You can purchase big prints for 4,900 yen.

10:45.478 --> 10:46.812
I'll take one, please.

10:46.896 --> 10:47.730
LIKED IT

10:50.316 --> 10:52.401
This is perfect for hiding our faces.

10:52.485 --> 10:54.111
<i>Soft to the touch too.</i>

10:54.195 --> 10:56.155
This way.

10:56.238 --> 10:59.200
There's a secret passage to the Lab
in the annex building.

10:59.742 --> 11:01.577
<i>I should come again with my family.</i>

11:04.163 --> 11:05.456
ORANGES

11:07.083 --> 11:09.168
-Untie me!
-Keep it down!

11:14.006 --> 11:15.841
<i>What is this place?</i>

11:15.925 --> 11:17.218
Mr. Tanaka.

11:17.301 --> 11:18.386
Yes, sir.

11:19.929 --> 11:23.099
Is that the boy with telepathic abilities?

11:24.266 --> 11:25.184
Yes…

11:26.477 --> 11:30.856
The hair color and gender
seem to be different from the photo…

11:30.940 --> 11:33.692
You know what happens
if you lie to the Reindeer, right?

11:35.569 --> 11:36.862
I'll kill you.

11:37.530 --> 11:39.156
Yes, sir.

11:39.740 --> 11:43.536
<i>What the… His hands and face</i>
<i>have stitches all over them.</i>

11:43.619 --> 11:45.162
<i>How unsettling…</i>

11:45.246 --> 11:47.540
Uh, boss? May I?

11:48.040 --> 11:48.916
Yes, Mr. Seba?

11:49.667 --> 11:53.921
So, this one's a phony body double,
but I might know where the real one is.

11:54.004 --> 11:55.756
Seba?!

11:55.840 --> 11:56.966
APPLES

11:57.049 --> 11:58.342
You son of a gun!

11:58.426 --> 12:00.761
-Screw you, Seba!
-My butt hurts!

12:00.845 --> 12:03.931
You must capture that boy.

12:04.014 --> 12:06.559
We cannot disappoint <i>him.</i>

12:07.143 --> 12:10.312
I'm counting on you, Mr. Seba.

12:10.396 --> 12:13.065
M'kay, I'll see what I can do.

12:13.149 --> 12:15.568
Let me see if I still remember.

12:15.651 --> 12:18.571
I think we turn this clock to 8:20

12:21.240 --> 12:24.869
then tilt that brown bear's head
90 degrees to the left…

12:32.626 --> 12:34.044
I was right!

12:34.128 --> 12:36.046
<i>What an annoying contraption.</i>

12:36.630 --> 12:38.924
And O-ku-ta-bi.

12:40.801 --> 12:42.636
<i>Authentication failed.</i>

12:42.720 --> 12:44.680
What? They changed the password.

12:45.723 --> 12:49.268
<i>Error code 203. Possible intruder.</i>

12:49.351 --> 12:50.436
<i>Initiate elimination.</i>

12:56.066 --> 13:00.029
<i>First round, unsuccessful.</i>
<i>Continue to second round--</i>

13:12.750 --> 13:16.170
Mr. Sakamoto, have you ever fought
an actual bear?

13:16.253 --> 13:18.672
<i>I've been trained</i>
<i>in all types of animal combat.</i>

13:19.381 --> 13:21.634
<i>Phase one, system down.</i>

13:21.717 --> 13:23.511
<i>Initiating phase two.</i>

13:29.058 --> 13:30.059
The heck?!

13:34.855 --> 13:36.899
<i>Dinosaurs would be a first, though.</i>

13:40.152 --> 13:42.196
How can we possibly…

13:42.863 --> 13:44.198
<i>A moving dinosaur…</i>

13:46.575 --> 13:48.202
It's so cute!

13:48.994 --> 13:50.204
<i>I want to show Hana.</i>

13:50.287 --> 13:51.121
What?!

13:51.205 --> 13:53.999
We want to take it alive, minimal damage.

13:54.083 --> 13:55.793
What is wrong with you?

13:58.796 --> 14:01.215
<i>We gotta do something about that tail.</i>

14:02.758 --> 14:04.468
I see some kind of device in its head!

14:04.552 --> 14:07.596
Maybe your electric gun can take it out
without damaging it!

14:07.680 --> 14:09.390
<i>Brilliant idea, Shin.</i>

14:10.015 --> 14:11.016
<i>Brilliant?</i>

14:32.329 --> 14:33.998
Yes, it worked!

14:34.874 --> 14:38.294
<i>System rebooted.</i>
<i>Target engagement level, max.</i>

14:46.010 --> 14:47.136
Mr. Sakamoto!

14:59.732 --> 15:01.150
His gun!

15:05.446 --> 15:07.072
<i>This is getting annoying.</i>

15:08.782 --> 15:10.826
Scrap the plan of taking it alive.

15:43.442 --> 15:47.863
After all, the fact that they don't move
is what makes dinosaurs so fascinating.

15:48.447 --> 15:49.865
Whatever you say, sir.

15:52.201 --> 15:53.243
It's gone quiet.

15:53.911 --> 15:55.079
What was that?

15:55.162 --> 15:58.290
Could it have been the security system
at the entrance?

15:58.874 --> 16:02.419
Hey, you shitty scientists!
Get back to work.

16:02.503 --> 16:04.380
You have to let us rest.

16:04.463 --> 16:06.382
We haven't slept in three days.

16:06.465 --> 16:10.010
If you want to be freed,
get us those results!

16:10.094 --> 16:11.762
You good-for-nothing scientists!

16:12.513 --> 16:14.139
-Dr. Ishikawa!
-Dr. Ishikawa!

16:15.057 --> 16:18.519
Do you seriously think
this silly research could ever succeed?

16:19.103 --> 16:20.521
"This silly research"?

16:21.188 --> 16:24.274
You let your mouth run a little too much.

16:24.858 --> 16:27.277
For your disrespect
toward the organization,

16:27.361 --> 16:28.195
you'll die!

16:35.035 --> 16:36.036
Hey.

16:36.120 --> 16:39.289
I know it's been a while,
but what the heck's going on?

16:39.873 --> 16:40.708
Shin!

16:40.791 --> 16:41.917
It's Shin.

16:42.001 --> 16:43.293
You came back?

16:44.044 --> 16:45.879
I had some business here.

16:45.963 --> 16:47.047
Where's the old man?

16:47.673 --> 16:50.467
The director has been locked up
in the lowest floor.

16:50.551 --> 16:54.763
The Lab has been taken over
by an assassin group.

16:55.431 --> 16:56.598
An assassin group?

16:57.725 --> 17:00.602
They appeared out of the blue,
about a year ago.

17:02.229 --> 17:03.731
Nice to meet you all.

17:03.814 --> 17:09.111
My name is Kashima. I'm a hit man.

17:09.695 --> 17:14.283
We are looking to innovate
our means of assassination.

17:14.366 --> 17:16.577
Guns and knives are things of the past.

17:17.161 --> 17:20.873
We'd like to incorporate the newest tech
in killing too.

17:21.373 --> 17:25.836
That's where we need the help
of your brilliant minds.

17:25.919 --> 17:28.922
<i>Kashima's the boss</i>
<i>who's at the center of everything.</i>

17:29.006 --> 17:32.342
<i>There are a few other leaders,</i>
<i>then the henchmen in hazmat suits.</i>

17:32.843 --> 17:34.595
I had no idea…

17:35.095 --> 17:38.766
Mr. Sakamoto, if we're going
to comb through this place to find Lu…

17:39.266 --> 17:41.769
We'll probably have to fight them, yes.

17:42.352 --> 17:43.604
What are you thinking?!

17:43.687 --> 17:45.939
You two have to get out of here fast.

17:46.023 --> 17:48.025
The leader in charge of this floor is--

17:51.820 --> 17:52.946
Here he comes! Hide!

17:53.030 --> 17:53.864
Hurry!

17:54.448 --> 17:55.783
Don't just stand there!

18:02.122 --> 18:03.749
I don't wanna be a guinea pig!

18:03.832 --> 18:06.418
Please! At least let <i>me</i> out!

18:06.502 --> 18:07.753
Stop whining already!

18:09.338 --> 18:12.382
How mean. You barbaric woman.

18:13.383 --> 18:16.011
What is that you've been doing anyway?

18:16.553 --> 18:19.431
Isn't it obvious?
I'm breaking out of this cell!

18:19.515 --> 18:22.226
Huh? Using that little rock?

18:22.309 --> 18:23.852
You've got to be kidding me.

18:23.936 --> 18:26.522
He's right, little lady.

18:27.022 --> 18:28.482
You don't want to do that.

18:29.775 --> 18:31.610
Who are you, old man?

18:32.236 --> 18:34.947
I'm Asakura, the director of this place.

18:35.531 --> 18:38.450
Could I interest you two
in a little prison break?

18:45.040 --> 18:47.209
What's all the excitement over here?

18:47.292 --> 18:50.003
We having some fun with an experiment?

18:50.087 --> 18:51.463
LEADER, MAD HORIGUCHI

18:52.131 --> 18:53.966
You have to let me join.

18:54.550 --> 18:55.801
No, there's nothing.

18:56.969 --> 18:59.680
Mind if I borrow your pen?

19:04.143 --> 19:05.060
Liar.

19:07.646 --> 19:09.106
<i>That bastard!</i>

19:09.189 --> 19:10.607
<i>I'm stuck…</i>

19:10.691 --> 19:13.861
One of my guys over there's passed out.

19:13.944 --> 19:16.613
What're you kids hiding, hmm?

19:17.948 --> 19:20.325
So? Who's gonna tell me?

19:20.409 --> 19:22.077
Pens out, everyone!

19:27.457 --> 19:29.376
See? I knew it.

19:31.253 --> 19:33.380
Good reflexes for an old guy like you.

19:33.964 --> 19:36.466
You idiot! Why did you come out?

19:37.926 --> 19:38.844
No reason.

19:41.346 --> 19:44.266
I don't like small spaces.

19:46.185 --> 19:47.019
Shin…

19:47.686 --> 19:49.104
Are you one of the leaders?

19:50.147 --> 19:52.149
What if I am?

19:52.232 --> 19:54.318
Are you going to get in our way?

19:54.818 --> 19:56.236
That won't do!

19:56.820 --> 19:59.615
This is some marvelous research
we're doing here!

20:00.824 --> 20:03.493
Here, let me show you myself!

20:17.090 --> 20:17.966
Shin!

20:19.343 --> 20:22.512
All right! Time for a lovely experiment!

20:23.805 --> 20:24.806
OW, THAT HURT!

20:24.890 --> 20:25.933
YOU JERK!

20:26.016 --> 20:27.017
WHAT?

20:29.686 --> 20:32.940
Great, isn't it?
A switch that switches around your words.

20:33.023 --> 20:36.193
I've embedded a needle in your head
that transmits a current,

20:36.276 --> 20:39.446
messing up the signals in your brain.

20:39.529 --> 20:40.948
WHAT THE HELL?

20:41.031 --> 20:41.949
FIX THIS NOW!

20:45.827 --> 20:47.246
Next, let's try… Oh?

20:58.298 --> 20:59.383
Finally got out.

20:59.466 --> 21:00.634
MR. SAKAMOTO!!

21:00.717 --> 21:02.886
Huh? Looks like you're having fun.

21:02.970 --> 21:05.138
DON'T MAKE FUN OF ME!!

21:06.974 --> 21:07.808
Shin,

21:08.725 --> 21:11.645
I don't know what happened in your past.

21:11.728 --> 21:14.147
But do you want to save this place?

21:16.483 --> 21:17.651
I DO…

21:18.527 --> 21:19.444
Okay, then.

21:20.070 --> 21:22.656
Time to clean up your childhood home.

21:22.739 --> 21:23.949
YES, SIR!

21:27.202 --> 21:30.998
I haven't taken a bus in ages.
My back hurts.

21:31.081 --> 21:33.959
Mr. Shishiba, let's eat these.

21:34.042 --> 21:35.752
Ah, your good-luck ritual.

21:37.212 --> 21:41.008
Honestly, are we sure
this place has something to do with Slur?

21:41.091 --> 21:44.511
Nagumo's not the most reliable chap,
is he?

21:44.594 --> 21:47.514
Investigating that is part of our job.

21:48.098 --> 21:50.851
Fair enough. Ready, Osaragi?

21:50.934 --> 21:51.768
Yes.

23:22.692 --> 23:25.779
Subtitle translation by: Yuka Kristi
